<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes" ?>
<cp:coreProperties xmlns:cp="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/package/2006/metadata/core-properties" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" xmlns:dcmitype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:dcterms="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance">
  <cp:category>model</cp:category>
  <cp:contentStatus>Exported from R2024b to R2024a</cp:contentStatus>
  <dcterms:created xsi:type="dcterms:W3CDTF">2003-05-19T13:24:40Z</dcterms:created>
  <dc:creator>The MathWorks, Inc.</dc:creator>
  <dc:description>
    
        R52 Mathworks Model PIL Block EBT
    
    
    
        R52 Mathworks Model PIL Block EBT
        &lt;a href="matlab:open(fullfile(mbd_find_s32ze_root(),'S32ZE_Examples\r52\pil\s32ze_model_pil_block\model_pil_block_simulink_r52.slx'))"&gt;Open Example
        The model_pil_block_simulink_r52.slx example illustrates the Reference Model PIL (Processor-in-the-Loop) simulation.
        
            This example shows you how to use Embedded Coder® Support Package for ARM Cortex-R™ Processors for code verification and validation using PIL.
        
            Note: the initialization settings for the components used in this example represent just a default EB Tresos available configuration.Users can change the configuration of the application to fit special requirements.
        
        Toolchain Supported
        
            
                S32 Design Studio v3.5.13
            
        
        Required Hardware
        
            
                Personal Computer
            
                S32Z2xx/S32E2xx
            
                12V Power Supply
            
                Micro USB cable
            
                S32 Debugger probe
            
        
        Prepare the Demo
        
            
                Open the model and select the processor package. This model is configured for the S32E2xx-bga975 hardware package. If you would like to change the processor package, please follow the steps described in the Customization Options section.
            
                Connect the S32 Debugger probe to the J129 JTAG pin connector on the EVB.
            
                Open the Hardware Settings of the model, go to Hardware Implementation -&gt; Target hardware resources -&gt; PIL tab.
            
                For the Serial Port option, type the COM Port as identified inside Device Manager under the Ports tab.
            
                UART default configuration is using the LINFLEXD instance 9 which is also used for serial boot on S32E27X-DC4 EVB. Disable the BootROM to be able to use the serial.
            
        
        Running the Demo
        
            
                To validate this example, follow the steps from Code Verification and Validation with PIL page, &lt;a href="https://www.mathworks.com/help/supportpkg/armcortexm/ref/code-verification-and-validation-with-pil-and-external-mode.html"&gt;Task 2 - Verify referenced model code using PIL
            
                For starting the PIL simulation open the SIL/PIL Manager from the Apps tab.
            
                From the SIL/PIL Manager App set the System Under Test to Model blocks in SIL/PIL mode.
            
                Press the Run Verification button. 
            
        
        Customization Options
		
            
                How to change the processor package - visit section 6.8 of &lt;a href="matlab:web(fullfile(mbd_find_s32ze_root(), 'mbdtbx_s32ze', 'help', 'release_notes.html'), '-browser')"&gt;Model_Based_Design_Toolbox_S32ZE_Series_Release_Notes
            
                How to create a configuration project for a custom board - visit section 6.6 of &lt;a href="matlab:web(fullfile(mbd_find_s32ze_root(), 'mbdtbx_s32ze', 'help', 'release_notes.html'), '-browser')"&gt;Model_Based_Design_Toolbox_S32ZE_Series_Release_Notes
            
                For S32Z and S32E Design Tools and Files, please visit &lt;a href="https://www.nxp.com/products/processors-and-microcontrollers/s32-automotive-platform/s32z-and-s32e-real-time-processors:S32Z-E-REAL-TIME-PROCESSORS"&gt;S32ZE Microcontrollers
            
        
    
    
    
</dc:description>
  <cp:lastModifiedBy>nxg00842</cp:lastModifiedBy>
